## 14. Local Service Discovery (LSD)

### What LSD Is

Local Service Discovery (BEP 14) allows BitTorrent clients on the same local network (LAN/WiFi) to find each other without going through a tracker. This is useful for campus networks, office networks, or home networks where multiple people are downloading the same file.

### How It Works

Your client periodically sends a multicast UDP message to `239.192.152.143:6771` (IPv4) or `[ff15::efc0:988f]:6771` (IPv6):

```
BT-SEARCH * HTTP/1.1\r\n
Host: 239.192.152.143:6771\r\n
Port: <your_listening_port>\r\n
Infohash: <info_hash_hex>\r\n
cookie: <random_32bit_int>\r\n
\r\n\r\n
```

Any client on the same LAN that is downloading the same torrent receives this multicast, sees the matching info hash, and connects to you directly. LAN transfer speeds are typically 100 Mbps to 1 Gbps — orders of magnitude faster than internet speeds.

